  "summary": "A common resident. Adults have all-black bodies. The male has a small crest on the forehead. The wings are grey-brown and speckled, the facial skin is yellow to reddish, the eyes are ruby-red and the bill is yellow. The brownish immature has off-white underparts, never pure white, and a more buffy upper breast. Newman says the illustrated female is a sub-adult that can breed. Newman does not describe the voice. The Kemp code RB was left unchanged.",
